                            <comment id="15832905" author="githubbot" created="Sat, 21 Jan 2017 09:21:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user astroshim opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1927&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1927&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1994&quot; title=&quot;Streaming output problem from the second run on PySpark.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-1994&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-1994&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; bugfix of streaming output.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    If you run the following code, then streaming output doesn&apos;t work properly from the second run.&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    %spark.pyspark&lt;br/&gt;
    import time&lt;br/&gt;
    print(&quot;1&quot;)&lt;br/&gt;
    time.sleep(2)&lt;br/&gt;
    print(&quot;2&quot;)&lt;br/&gt;
    time.sleep(2)&lt;br/&gt;
    print(&quot;3&quot;)&lt;br/&gt;
    time.sleep(2)&lt;br/&gt;
    print(&quot;4&quot;)&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    This problem comes from the order of `paragraph update` event timing and `paragraph update-append` event timing is incorrect.&lt;br/&gt;
    and This PR will fix also &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1833&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1833&lt;/a&gt; too.&lt;/li&gt;
